Reinsurance capital today: a static pot allocated behind closed doors.

The alternative: pools that can be tranched, tokenized, and traded.

@karnsaroya on how onchain capital fits into reinsurance: https://t.co/N64kvjfRui

Galaxy’s $100M sUSDS allocation followed institutional due diligence.

@John__Conneely explains how @galaxyhq examined Sky Protocol’s mechanics and risk management through the scrutiny it applies to traditional assets.

Watch the clip ↓ https://t.co/VpzkMYfUhQ

Liquidity is central to institutional confidence in sUSDS.

At the time of recording, $8.9B of Sky Protocol’s $9.63B in allocations was redeemable within a week.

@gregfeibus explains the liquidity waterfall with @Game_Set_Max of @galaxyhq on @MilkRoadDaily ↓ https://t.co/Fddz3xb1U4

Capital discipline builds institutional trust.

@RuneKek explains Sky Protocol’s focus on building capital buffers, improving transparency and increasing efficiency, rather than taking on more risk to chase market share.

Watch the clip ↓ https://t.co/aaMsLmwUx5

“Laniakea is going to allow Sky Ecosystem to scale to any level.”

@RuneKek explains how the upgrade is designed to streamline institutional connectivity while keeping risk transparent and complexity under control as the network grows.

Watch the full clip ↓ https://t.co/zqqdTbw3ZF

“A year ago, operating expenses were above $20M. This quarter, they are down to $6.8M.”

@RuneKek explains how the Sky Treasury Management Function has made operating expenses more predictable and bounded while supporting security, maintenance and development.

Watch ↓ https://t.co/6XQJf2MTuz

“Blockchain’s killer use case is openness: it drives competition on pricing and makes financial infrastructure more accessible. 

At Morpho, we use that openness to collapse the spread between lending and borrowing rates.” 

@PaulFrambot on stage with @ethereumJoseph @SamirTabar @kartiktalwar at @token2049

